    "b-50-knowledge-model-the-scheduler-gets-ranki-7": {
      "id": "b-50-knowledge-model-the-scheduler-gets-ranki-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The scheduler gets ranking inputs from the graph and applies explicit epoch\npolicy. Workers get one compact operating guide by default. Capability hints add focused lookup,\nmatching, or last-resort sweep context only when the packet needs it. The\none-symbol targeted iteration loop is part of the worker system prompt, not a\nseparate knowledge workflow."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-knowledge-model-this-keeps-the-default-w-8": {
      "id": "b-50-knowledge-model-this-keeps-the-default-w-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "This keeps the default worker posture careful and evidence-backed. Broader\nexperimental search and permuter handoff enter only when a packet or capability\nroute asks for compact last-resort sweep context."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-knowledge-model-naming-guided-search-9": {
      "id": "b-50-knowledge-model-naming-guided-search-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Naming-Guided Search"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-knowledge-model-worker-search-is-thought-10": {
      "id": "b-50-knowledge-model-worker-search-is-thought-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Worker search is thoughtful, not random. A worker should use the target symbol,\nsource path, nearby matched code, headers, splits, symbols, PR history, and\nresource tables to infer likely names the original developer would have used:\nstruct fields, callbacks, states, helper functions, data owners, and sibling\nfiles. Each new fact should narrow the next search query or suggest another\nspecific file to inspect."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-knowledge-model-when-those-evidence-back-11": {
      "id": "b-50-knowledge-model-when-those-evidence-back-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "When those evidence-backed names and paths run out, the worker should stop\nbefore hard guessing. The next useful move is to identify what missing fact\nwould make the search grounded again, queue fact research, or move the worker\nslot to a more constrained target."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-knowledge-model-resource-contract-12": {
      "id": "b-50-knowledge-model-resource-contract-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Resource Contract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-knowledge-model-knowledge-material-shoul-13": {
      "id": "b-50-knowledge-model-knowledge-material-shoul-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Knowledge material should make agents better at choosing grounded next moves.\nIt should not swamp prompts with the whole repository or encourage random\nsweeps. Useful knowledge names exact sources, explains when it applies, and\npreserves provenance so facts can be checked later."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
